==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|fro|surcengle|}}, formed with {{m|fr|sur||over}} and {{m|fro|cengle||girdle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɜːsɪŋɡ(ə)l/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɜɹˌsɪŋ.ɡəl/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Gibraltar Rocks-surcingle.wav|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A long unpadded strap to pass over and keep in place a blanket, pack or [[saddle]] on an animal.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1929|author=Baldwyn Dyke Acland|title=Filibuster|chapter=8|edition=|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL219110W|passage=He was standing on the offside of his horse, holding up the flap of his saddle, with the '''surcingle''' loosened, and was pointing to the [[girth#Noun|girths]]. Close to their attachment to the saddle they had been almost cut through with a knife.}}
# A piece of [[tack]] wrapped around the belly of a horse, to use when [[longe]]ing.
# A [[girdle]] to fasten a garment, especially a [[cassock]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|circingle}}
